        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nodelet>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/roscpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/stereo-image-proc> ;
    ros:supportsHardware hw:Camera ;
    rdfs:comment "Package: avt_vimba_camera | Description: Camera driver for Allied Vision Technologies (AVT) cameras, based on their Vimba SDK. | Function: Provides a ROS interface for Allied Vision Technologies (AVT) cameras using the Vimba SDK, publishing image frames and supporting Ethernet‑based triggering and precise timestamping via PTP. | Use Cases: Real‑time image acquisition for perception pipelines, Triggering frame captures over Ethernet for synchronized multi‑sensor setups, Precise timestamping of images using PTP for time‑critical applications | Hardware Required: Allied Vision Technologies (AVT) camera | Hardware Supported: AVT GigE cameras (e.g., Mako, other GigE models), AVT USB cameras (if supported by the Vimba SDK) | Performance: GigE cameras may generate high bandwidth streams; it is recommended to set the network MTU to 9014 and increase the receive buffer to 26214400 for reliable operation. These settings have been verified to work with AVT cameras. | Categories: perception"^^xsd:string,
        "Performance: GigE cameras may generate high bandwidth streams; it is recommended to set the network MTU to 9014 and increase the receive buffer to 26214400 for reliable operation. These settings have been verified to work with AVT cameras."^^xsd:string .

