        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros> ;
    rdfs:comment "Package: realsense2_camera | Description: RealSense camera package allowing access to Intel D400 3D cameras | Function: Provides a ROS2 wrapper for Intel RealSense D400 series 3D cameras, exposing RGB, depth, infrared, point‑cloud, and metadata streams as ROS topics, services, and actions while allowing runtime configuration of sensors and post‑processing filters. | Use Cases: Depth perception for robotic manipulation, 3‑D mapping and scene reconstruction, Object detection and segmentation pipelines, SLAM input for navigation, AR/VR applications requiring depth data, Vision‑based robot navigation | Algorithms: Depth alignment, Point cloud generation, Post‑processing filters (e.g., denoising, decimation), Extrinsics calibration, Frame transformation (TF publishing) | Hardware Required: Intel RealSense D400 series camera (e.g., D435, D435i, D455), USB 3.0 connection | Hardware Supported: Intel RealSense D400 series (D435, D435i, D455, D465), Intel RealSense L500 series | Performance: Supports efficient intra‑process communication and allows runtime enabling/disabling of sensors and post‑processing blocks, providing low‑latency streaming suitable for real‑time robotic applications. | Categories: perception"^^xsd:string,
        "Performance: Supports efficient intra‑process communication and allows runtime enabling/disabling of sensors and post‑processing blocks, providing low‑latency streaming suitable for real‑time robotic applications."^^xsd:string .

