    rdfs:comment "Package: sick_scan | Description: ROS 1 and 2 driver for SICK scanner | Function: Driver providing ROS 1 and ROS 2 support for SICK LiDAR and Radar sensors, with generic C/C++ and Python APIs for data acquisition and integration. | Use Cases: Acquiring LiDAR point‑cloud data for SLAM and mapping applications, Running SLAM algorithms such as Hector SLAM, Google Cartographer, and RTAB‑Map, Integrating LiDAR data with IMU and encoder information for navigation, Radar sensing for obstacle detection and tracking, Deploying multi‑sensor setups (e.g., multiple LiDARs or LiDAR+Radar), Using the driver in both ROS and non‑ROS environments via generic APIs, Testing and simulating LiDAR data with provided tools | Algorithms: SLAM, Google Cartographer, RTAB-Map, OctoMap | Hardware Required: SICK LiDAR, SICK Radar | Hardware Supported: picoScan100, multiScan100, TiMxxx, NAV350, MRS6124, LMS1000, MRS1000, RMS1000, MRS6000, LRS4000 | Performance: Optimized for x64 and ARM64 architectures, but experiences performance limitations on Raspberry Pi models; no external dependencies such as Boost reduce runtime overhead. | Categories: perception, navigation, mapping"^^xsd:string,
        "Performance: Optimized for x64 and ARM64 architectures, but experiences performance limitations on Raspberry Pi models; no external dependencies such as Boost reduce runtime overhead."^^xsd:string .

<http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/spatio-temporal-voxel-layer> a ros:MappingPackage,
        ros:NavigationPackage,
        ros:PerceptionPackage,
        ros:ROSPackage ;
    rdfs:label "Spatio Temporal Voxel Layer"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:description "The spatio-temporal 3D obstacle costmap package"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: RoboCup@Home competitions"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: dynamic indoor mapping and obstacle avoidance"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: factory floor mapping and navigation"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: hospitality service robots"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: library and hospital robot assistance"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: oil and gas facility inspection"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: retail environment navigation"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: warehouse automation"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:buildDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/builtin-interfaces>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/laser-geometry>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libopenexr-dev>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libpcl-all-dev>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/message-filters>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav2-costmap-2d>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav2-ros-common>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/openvdb-vendor>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/pcl-conversions>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/pluginlib>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/point-cloud-transport>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/point-cloud-transport-plugins>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rclcpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rosidl-default-generators>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-srvs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/visualization-msgs> ;
    ros:distribution "humble"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:implementsAlgorithm "approximate voxel grid filtering to reduce measurement spikes"^^xsd:string,
        "frustum‑based voxel acceleration for depth cameras and 3‑D LiDARs"^^xsd:string,
        "spatio‑temporal voxel grid representation"^^xsd:string,
        "voxel decay with configurable decay functions"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:lastUpdated "2025-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    ros:licenseType "LGPL v2.1"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:maintainer "Steve Macenski <stevenmacenski@gmail.com>"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:optionallyDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-lint-auto> ;
    ros:packageName "spatio_temporal_voxel_layer"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:packageVersion "2.6.0"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:primaryFunction "A ROS costmap layer that represents the 3‑D environment using a spatio‑temporal voxel grid backed by OpenVDB, providing efficient sparse voxel storage, dynamic obstacle handling via voxel decay, and real‑time 3‑D mapping for navigation."^^xsd:string ;
    ros:repositoryURL "https://github.com/SteveMacenski/spatio_temporal_voxel_layer"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ros:requiresHardware hw:Camera,
        hw:LaserScanner ;
    ros:rosVersion "ROS 2"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:runtimeDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/builtin-interfaces>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/laser-geometry>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libopenexr-dev>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libpcl-all-dev>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/message-filters>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav2-costmap-2d>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav2-ros-common>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/openvdb-vendor>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/pcl-conversions>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/pluginlib>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/point-cloud-transport>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/point-cloud-transport-plugins>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rclcpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rosidl-default-runtime>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-srvs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/visualization-msgs> ;
    ros:supportsHardware hw:Camera,
        hw:LaserScanner ;
    rdfs:comment "Package: spatio_temporal_voxel_layer | Description: The spatio-temporal 3D obstacle costmap package | Function: A ROS costmap layer that represents the 3‑D environment using a spatio‑temporal voxel grid backed by OpenVDB, providing efficient sparse voxel storage, dynamic obstacle handling via voxel decay, and real‑time 3‑D mapping for navigation. | Use Cases: retail environment navigation, warehouse automation, factory floor mapping and navigation, library and hospital robot assistance, hospitality service robots, RoboCup@Home competitions, oil and gas facility inspection, dynamic indoor mapping and obstacle avoidance | Algorithms: spatio‑temporal voxel grid representation, voxel decay with configurable decay functions, frustum‑based voxel acceleration for depth cameras and 3‑D LiDARs, approximate voxel grid filtering to reduce measurement spikes | Hardware Required: depth camera(s) (e.g., Intel Realsense), 3‑D LiDAR (e.g., Velodyne VLP‑16), CPU (5th gen i7 or equivalent for real‑time performance) | Hardware Supported: any RGB‑D or stereo depth camera, any 3‑D LiDAR with vertical FOV (e.g., Velodyne, Ouster, etc.) | Performance: The layer operates on commodity CPUs; on a 5th‑gen i7, dense depth‑camera setups with 7 cameras reduced move_base CPU usage to 20–50 % of nominal (80–110 %) when using the approximate voxel filter. The filter adds only 1–2 % CPU overhead. Memory usage is low—about 6.5 MB for a 60,000 sq ft store at 0.05 m resolution. Decay times of 1–30 s for local costmaps and 15–45 s for global costmaps enable timely removal of obsolete voxels, supporting real‑time navigation. | Categories: perception, mapping, navigation, costmap"^^xsd:string,
        "Performance: The layer operates on commodity CPUs; on a 5th‑gen i7, dense depth‑camera setups with 7 cameras reduced move_base CPU usage to 20–50 % of nominal (80–110 %) when using the approximate voxel filter. The filter adds only 1–2 % CPU overhead. Memory usage is low—about 6.5 MB for a 60,000 sq ft store at 0.05 m resolution. Decay times of 1–30 s for local costmaps and 15–45 s for global costmaps enable timely removal of obsolete voxels, supporting real‑time navigation."^^xsd:string .

