<http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/robot-state-publisher> a ros:NavigationPackage,
        ros:PerceptionPackage,
        ros:ROSPackage ;
    rdfs:label "Robot State Publisher"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:description """
    This package take the joint angles of a robot as input, and publishes the 3D poses of the robot links to tf2, using a kinematic tree model of the robot.
  """^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: Facilitating the integration of robot description models (URDF) with runtime joint state updates."^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: Providing tf transforms for robot kinematics to enable motion planning, control, and simulation."^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: Serving as the source of joint state information for other ROS nodes that rely on tf for coordinate transformations."^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: Visualizing robot state and kinematic chains in RViz or other visualization tools."^^xsd:string ;
    ros:buildDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/builtin-interfaces>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/kdl-parser>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/liborocos-kdl-dev>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rcl-interfaces>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rclcpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rclcpp-components>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/urdf> ;
    ros:distribution "humble"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:lastUpdated "2025-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    ros:licenseType "BSD"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:maintainer "Chris Lalancette <clalancette@openrobotics.org>"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:optionallyDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-cmake-gtest>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-lint-auto>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-lint-common>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/launch-ros>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/launch-testing-ament-cmake>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros-py> ;
    ros:packageName "robot_state_publisher"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:packageVersion "3.5.3"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:primaryFunction "Publishes the state of a robot by converting joint states into 3D transforms and broadcasting them over tf2."^^xsd:string ;
    ros:repositoryURL "https://github.com/ros/robot_state_publisher"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ros:rosVersion "ROS 2"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:runtimeDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/builtin-interfaces>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/kdl-parser>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/liborocos-kdl>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rcl-interfaces>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rclcpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rclcpp-components>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/urdf> ;
    rdfs:comment """Package: robot_state_publisher | Description: 
    This package take the joint angles of a robot as input, and publishes the 3D poses of the robot links to tf2, using a kinematic tree model of the robot.
   | Function: Publishes the state of a robot by converting joint states into 3D transforms and broadcasting them over tf2. | Use Cases: Providing tf transforms for robot kinematics to enable motion planning, control, and simulation., Visualizing robot state and kinematic chains in RViz or other visualization tools., Serving as the source of joint state information for other ROS nodes that rely on tf for coordinate transformations., Facilitating the integration of robot description models (URDF) with runtime joint state updates. | Performance: Static joint transforms are published once on startup to the `/tf_static` topic. Non‑static joint transforms are published at a maximum frequency specified by the `publish_frequency` parameter (default 20 Hz), with optional timestamp handling controlled by `ignore_timestamp`. | Categories: navigation, perception"""^^xsd:string,
        "Performance: Static joint transforms are published once on startup to the `/tf_static` topic. Non‑static joint transforms are published at a maximum frequency specified by the `publish_frequency` parameter (default 20 Hz), with optional timestamp handling controlled by `ignore_timestamp`."^^xsd:string .

<http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/slam-toolbox> a ros:LocalizationPackage,
