    ros:licenseType "LGPL"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:maintainer "Michel Hidalgo <michel@ekumenlabs.com>"^^xsd:string,
        "Steve Macenski <stevenmacenski@gmail.com>"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:optionallyDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-cmake-cpplint>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-cmake-flake8>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-cmake-gtest>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-cmake-uncrustify>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/ament-lint-auto>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/launch>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/launch-testing> ;
    ros:packageName "slam_toolbox"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:packageVersion "2.9.0"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:primaryFunction "A 2D SLAM and localization library that builds and optimizes pose-graph maps from laser scans and odometry, supporting real‑time mapping, life‑long and multi‑robot mapping."^^xsd:string ;
    ros:repositoryURL "https://github.com/SteveMacenski/slam_toolbox"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ros:requiresHardware hw:IMU,
        hw:LaserScanner ;
    ros:rosVersion "ROS 2"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:runtimeDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/bond>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/bondcpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/boost>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/builtin-interfaces>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/eigen>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/interactive-markers>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libceres-dev>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/liblapack-dev>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libomp-dev>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libqt5-core>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libqt5-gui>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libqt5-opengl>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/libqt5-widgets>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/lifecycle-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/message-filters>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav2-map-server>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/pluginlib>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rclcpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rclcpp-lifecycle>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rosidl-default-generators>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rosidl-default-runtime>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rviz-common>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rviz-default-plugins>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rviz-ogre-vendor>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rviz-rendering>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-srvs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/suitesparse>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tbb>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/visualization-msgs> ;
    ros:supportsHardware hw:LaserScanner,
        hw:WheelEncoder ;
    rdfs:comment """Package: slam_toolbox | Description: 
     This package provides a sped up improved slam karto with updated SDK and visualization and modification toolsets
   | Function: A 2D SLAM and localization library that builds and optimizes pose-graph maps from laser scans and odometry, supporting real‑time mapping, life‑long and multi‑robot mapping. | Use Cases: Retail store mapping, Warehouse inventory and navigation, Library environment mapping, Research robot navigation, Life‑long mapping of dynamic indoor spaces, Multi‑robot collaborative mapping, Large‑scale indoor mapping up to several hundred thousand square feet | Algorithms: Pose‑graph SLAM, Laser scan matching, Loop closure detection, Graph optimization (Google Ceres plugin), Synchronous and asynchronous mapping, Elastic graph manipulation merging (in progress), Optimization‑based localization | Hardware Required: 2D laser scanner (lidar), odometry source (wheel encoders, IMU or equivalent), ROS 2 runtime | Hardware Supported: Any 2D lidar, including 360° and non‑axially mounted sensors, Any robot platform that provides odometry, Multi‑robot setups with shared global frame | Performance: The package can build maps at 5× or more real‑time speed for areas up to ~30,000 sq ft, and 3× real‑time for up to ~60,000 sq ft. In synchronous mode it has mapped a 200,000 sq ft building, while asynchronous mode can handle even larger spaces. The snap package (slam‑toolbox) delivers roughly 10× faster performance compared to the source build. | Categories: mapping, localization, perception"""^^xsd:string,
        "Performance: The package can build maps at 5× or more real‑time speed for areas up to ~30,000 sq ft, and 3× real‑time for up to ~60,000 sq ft. In synchronous mode it has mapped a 200,000 sq ft building, while asynchronous mode can handle even larger spaces. The snap package (slam‑toolbox) delivers roughly 10× faster performance compared to the source build."^^xsd:string .

<http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/base-local-planner> a ros:ControlPackage,
        ros:MobileRobotPackage,
        ros:NavigationPackage,
        ros:ROSPackage ;
    rdfs:label "Base Local Planner"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:description """

        This package provides implementations of the Trajectory Rollout and Dynamic Window approaches to local robot navigation on a plane. Given a plan to follow and a costmap, the controller produces velocity commands to send to a mobile base. This package supports both holonomic and non-holonomic robots, any robot footprint that can be represented as a convex polygon or circle, and exposes its configuration as ROS parameters that can be set in a launch file. This package's ROS wrapper adheres to the BaseLocalPlanner interface specified in the """^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: 2D local navigation of mobile robots within the ROS navigation stack"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: generating velocity commands for a mobile base from a costmap and global plan"^^xsd:string,
        "Use case: obstacle avoidance and safe navigation in planar environments"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:buildDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/angles>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/cmake-modules>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/costmap-2d>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/dynamic-reconfigure>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/eigen>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/message-generation>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav-core>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/pluginlib>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rosconsole>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/roscpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rospy>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/visualization-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/voxel-grid> ;
    ros:distribution "humble"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:implementsAlgorithm "Dynamic Window"^^xsd:string,
        "Trajectory Rollout"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:lastUpdated "2025-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    ros:licenseType "BSD"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:maintainer "Aaron Hoy <ahoy@fetchrobotics.com>"^^xsd:string,
        "David V. Lu!! <davidvlu@gmail.com>"^^xsd:string,
        "Michael Ferguson <mfergs7@gmail.com>"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:optionallyDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rosunit> ;
    ros:packageName "base_local_planner"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:packageVersion "1.17.3"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:primaryFunction "Provides a local robot navigation controller that generates velocity commands from a plan and costmap using Trajectory Rollout and Dynamic Window approaches."^^xsd:string ;
    ros:repositoryURL "https://github.com/ros-planning/navigation"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ros:rosVersion "ROS 2"^^xsd:string ;
    ros:runtimeDependsOn <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/angles>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/costmap-2d>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/dynamic-reconfigure>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/eigen>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/geometry-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/message-runtime>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav-core>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/nav-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/pluginlib>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rosconsole>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/roscpp>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/rospy>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/sensor-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/std-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/tf2-ros>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/visualization-msgs>,
        <http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/voxel-grid> ;
    rdfs:comment """Package: base_local_planner | Description: 

        This package provides implementations of the Trajectory Rollout and Dynamic Window approaches to local robot navigation on a plane. Given a plan to follow and a costmap, the controller produces velocity commands to send to a mobile base. This package supports both holonomic and non-holonomic robots, any robot footprint that can be represented as a convex polygon or circle, and exposes its configuration as ROS parameters that can be set in a launch file. This package's ROS wrapper adheres to the BaseLocalPlanner interface specified in the  | Function: Provides a local robot navigation controller that generates velocity commands from a plan and costmap using Trajectory Rollout and Dynamic Window approaches. | Use Cases: 2D local navigation of mobile robots within the ROS navigation stack, generating velocity commands for a mobile base from a costmap and global plan, obstacle avoidance and safe navigation in planar environments | Algorithms: Trajectory Rollout, Dynamic Window | Hardware Supported: holonomic mobile base, non-holonomic mobile base | Categories: navigation, control"""^^xsd:string .

<http://www.ros.org/ontology#package/cartographer> a ros:LocalizationPackage,
